  "details": "Some avatars go invisible, but it's hard to implement and also poses some comfort/safety issues. As they could be used for cheating in games or following people who don't know you're there, which most avatar creators don't want.\n\nI think it would be cool if this could be implemented at the SDK level.\n\nAs opposed to hiding the renderers traditionally, which leads to desync if not done in a strange way, an SDK-level implementation could integrate with Comfort & Safety.\n\nI imagine there would be a setting in the Comfort and Safety settings for \"Avatar Invisibility\" that would let you select between Allowed, Fallback Shown, and Disabled. Fallback Shown would show a generic robot avatar or some equivalent to indicate they're \"invisible\".\n\nThis would also allow invisibility toggles to work on Imposter fallbacks, so you don't need to show a person's avatar just for their invisibility gimmmick to work.\n\nMy proposed example is The Dissppearing Guy from TADC, an avatar I'm creating right now!",
